{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"FINISHED AND COMMITTED by the orchestrator — the implementing agent died twice to API errors, so\nrecording exactly what state it left and what I verified, rather than trusting either report.\n\n**WHAT IT LEFT:** a complete implementation, uncommitted. The first failure came mid-implementation\n(I sampled it then and got 10 failed / 9 passed, which I initially mistook for a broken restore); the\nsecond came after it had finished the code and both gates, with only the CLI suites left to run. So\nthe work was done, just never committed.\n\n**WHAT I VERIFIED MYSELF rather than taking on trust:**\n- the guard's own suite: **19/19 pass**;\n- **the tests have teeth** — stashing ONLY `src/` and `docs/` and re-running gives **13 failed /\n  6 passed**, and the 6 that stay green are the controls that must pass in both states. So the guard\n  is load-bearing, not incidental;\n- the broader CLI surface: **392 passed, 3 skipped** across everything matching\n  cli/command/comment/session_log/tag;\n- `make lint` clean, `make typecheck` clean (407 files).\n\n**A SECOND DEFECT THE AGENT FOUND that the ticket had not identified.** The failure was quiet because\nTWO bugs were stacked: the option-looking token was stored as the body, AND any surplus positional\nholding the intended value was dropped by an `args[:min_args]` slice. So\n`rebar comment <id> --body-file notes.md` lost the body twice over — once by storing the flag, once by\ndiscarding the path — and still exited 0. Only fixing the first would have left\n`rebar comment <id> <flag> <value>` still silently lossy.\n\n**SCOPE DELIVERED:** the audit the ticket asked for covered `create`, `edit` and `session-log`, and the\nguard now spans `comment`, `tag`, `untag`, `archive` and `set-verify-commands` — driven off a command\ntable carrying each one's arity and canonical `Usage:` line, so a new positional-only command inherits\nthe guard instead of having to remember it. `--` is the escape hatch for a value that legitimately\nbegins with `-`, and is tested on both the comment and tag paths. `comment` additionally prints the\n`\"$(cat file)\"` substitution hint, since a lost comment body is the motivating failure.\n\n**On the explicit \"decide whether to add a real `--body-file`\" criterion:** the implementation did NOT\nadd one; it made the positional form loud and documented the shell-substitution idiom instead. I am\nrecording that as the decision and its rationale rather than re-litigating it — but flagging for the\noperator that the ticket asked for an explicit decision either way, and the reasoning for choosing NOT\nto add the option is thinner in the record than the rest of the work. If a real `--body-file` is\nwanted, that is a small follow-up rather than a defect in this change.\n\n**One artifact caught at commit time:** the first commit accidentally included a `.provision.log` I had\ncreated while provisioning that worktree's venv. Amended out; the commit is 6 files, all intentional.\n\nGerrit change **1197**, stacked on the epic branch. Commit `ac24eacab`."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785634719261491001,"uuid":"ab0db3bd-ecca-44fb-8ab3-400930be2d16"}